8198	{"artifactId":"LLD-7aaf7e1b4a54e86f-s1","entry":{"id":"review-375e97ae948590f0595b28040f3be747","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-29T19:42:08.912Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design's root cause (operator path to produce installed qualification evidence is missing while qualifyInvestigationAdapter/production adoption only consume evidence) matches the ISSUE's stated rootCause and fixIntent, and the LLD's migration steps (1-5) and chosen alternative (8.1) cover every element of fixIntent: a bounded auditable probe via CliProvider, independently verifiable evidence, preserved independent trust/approval, and a path to real acceptance with activation signoff.","evidence":"ISSUE-7aaf7e1b4a54e86f.json body.rootCause: 'qualifyInvestigationAdapter validates supplied evidence; production adoption verifies its signature against an independently provisioned trust anchor... This leaves a bootstrap gap for real acceptance'; body.fixIntent: 'Provide a bounded, auditable operator acceptance path... Preserve independent trust and approval... Then execute real source-only and indexed acceptance... present activation evidence for user signoff.' Confirmed against src/daemon/review-investigation-adoption.ts (verifyInstalledProbeSignature reads an externally provisioned key at PATHS.insrc/review-probe-trust.pem, not generated by the daemon) and src/agent/providers/investigation-session.ts (qualifyInvestigationAdapter only validates supplied evidence, never produces it). The LLD's migration section and alternative 8.1 enumerate matching steps for each fixIntent element.","action":"None — the mapping between ISSUE fix intent and design migration/alternatives is complete and grounded in real code.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"qualifyInvestigationAdapter (2.3) validates only supplied evidence and, for installed-probe origin, requires an authority.verifyInstalled callback; production adoption (review-investigation-adoption.ts) supplies that callback bound to verifyInstalledProbeSignature, which reads a daemon-private key file that the daemon does not create — i.e. an independently provisioned trust anchor, exactly as the design's current-behaviour claims (2.3 Preconditions, 3.2 'Existing independently provisioned trust anchor').","evidence":"src/agent/providers/investigation-session.ts lines 98-101: `if(authority.origin==='installed-probe'){ if(!authority.verifyInstalled)refuse(...); await authority.verifyInstalled(reference,evidenceDigest); }`. src/daemon/review-investigation-adoption.ts lines 63-67 (verifyInstalledProbeSignature) opens `join(PATHS.insrc,'review-probe-trust.pem')` read-only with O_NOFOLLOW and verifies an Ed/ECDSA-style signature over the evidence; the key file is never written by this code path, matching 'Independent signing key is provisioned outside daemon; daemon never creates/copies private keys'.","action":"None — current-behaviour claims are accurate.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Data model 3.1's 'Call sites' list (cli-provider.ts, native-investigation-session.ts, review-investigation-adoption.ts) is the complete set of files needing change to add the new main-daemon IPC method `codeReview.investigation.probe`, as 3.1's own text claims ('The operation uses the existing main-daemon method routing...').","evidence":"The only place sibling investigation IPC methods are actually registered/dispatched is src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts (e.g. line 608: `'codeReview.investigation.capabilities': async()=>{...}`, line 612: `'codeReview.investigation': async params => {...}`) and src/daemon/threads/method-class.ts (lines 89-90, 283: method-class entries `['codeReview.investigation','session',false]`, `['codeReview.investigation.capabilities','session',false]`). A new `codeReview.investigation.probe` method needs an entry in both files to be routable at all, exactly like its siblings, but neither file appears in 3.1's call-site list. [files: src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/daemon/threads/method-class.ts]","action":"Add src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts and src/daemon/threads/method-class.ts to the 3.1 call-site list before build, or the new probe IPC method will be unroutable as scoped.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The signatures/types the design cites for CliProvider (2.1, `implements LLMProvider`) and nativeReviewMcpConfiguration (2.2, `(cwd:string,indexed:boolean)=>{mcpServers:...}`) match the real declarations.","evidence":"src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts line 190: `export class CliProvider implements LLMProvider {`. src/agent/providers/native-investigation-session.ts line 19: `export function nativeReviewMcpConfiguration(cwd:string,indexed:boolean){ ... return {mcpServers:{'insrc-scoped-review':{command:...,args:[...]}}}; }` — matches the design's description exactly, including reuse by claude-/codex-investigation-session.ts callers.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Invariant [[c2]] ('CLI model execution remains in CliProvider; no cloud REST, credential copying or production review authorization from probe grants') is real and the probe design as specified does not violate it: nativeInvestigationEnvironment already strips credential-bearing env vars and the probe design explicitly forbids arbitrary executable/paths/production binding through IPC.","evidence":"src/agent/providers/native-investigation-session.ts lines 24-27 (nativeInvestigationEnvironment) allowlists a fixed set of env vars (HOME, PATH, XDG_*, proxy vars, CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, CODEX_HOME) and excludes inherited plugins/hooks/NODE_OPTIONS/API keys, consistent with CLAUDE.md's 'No direct cloud REST calls from our process' rule and with the design's 2.1 Errors ('No arbitrary executable, args, prompt, paths or production binding may be supplied through IPC'). No code path in cli-provider.ts or investigation-session.ts performs a direct REST call.","action":"None — the invariant holds against current code and the design does not introduce a REST path.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion (ac1-ac5) is backed by a test that would fail without the fix.","evidence":"This is a standalone, not-yet-built Story (no HLD/build artifacts exist for epic 7aaf7e1b4a54e86f beyond this LLD and its parent ISSUE/EPIC). The cited test files for integration patterns do exist (src/daemon/__tests__/review-investigation-adoption.test.ts, src/mcp/__tests__/review-investigation-native-restart.test.ts, src/agent/providers/__tests__/native-investigation-fixtures.ts), confirming the test strategy is grounded in real existing suites/fixtures rather than invented paths, but the acceptance-mapping tests themselves (ac1-ac5 'Proving tests') name planned, not-yet-written tests, so I cannot run them against the fix to confirm they fail on main and pass post-fix.","action":"Verify ac1-ac5 proving tests at code-review/validate time once the Story is built, mapping each named test to real file+title per the build gate's `tests` contract.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":0,"low":5,"unverified":1},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-29T19:42:08.912Z","model":"cli-claude:claude-sonnet-5","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
