9243	{"artifactId":"LLD-7aaf7e1b4a54e86f-s1","entry":{"id":"review-764faa25e5cbc6ad00e405da126c8542","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-29T19:45:08.356Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design's migration plan (section 7) and acceptance mapping (ac1-ac5) cover every element the ISSUE's fixIntent names: a bounded auditable operator probe through the installed CLI, independently verifiable effective-inventory/denial evidence, durable progress+cancellation proof, installation/configuration pins, explicit unsupported outcomes, preserved independent trust/approval (no auto-signoff), then real source-only+indexed acceptance with observed accounting and activation signoff, while legacy CODE review stays until acceptance+signoff.","evidence":"ISSUE-7aaf7e1b4a54e86f.json body.fixIntent: 'Provide a bounded, auditable operator acceptance path... Collect independently verifiable effective inventory and denied-access evidence, durable progress and cancellation, installation/configuration pins, and explicit unsupported outcomes. Preserve independent trust and approval... Then execute real source-only and indexed acceptance... Keep legacy CODE review until acceptance and explicit signoff.' The LLD's Migration steps 1-5 and acceptance-mapping ac1-ac5 reproduce each clause (probe deploy -> observation attempts -> independent verification/signing -> normal-admission bounded acceptance with opt-in -> legacy deletion deferred as separate tracked change) with no fixIntent clause left unaddressed. [files: .insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-7aaf7e1b4a54e86f.json]","action":"None — the planned scope matches the issue's stated fix intent.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"qualifyInvestigationAdapter exists today with the exact signature and verification behaviour the LLD describes (signed-evidence-only input, identity/catalog/digest checks, ISOLATION_DENIAL_PROBES coverage, two-ACK + cancel/exit proof, and installed-probe vs scripted-fixture origin dispatch), and nativeReviewMcpConfiguration(cwd, indexed) exists returning the scoped MCP server launch config as claimed.","evidence":"src/agent/providers/investigation-session.ts:85-100 defines `export async function qualifyInvestigationAdapter(reference, expected, repoPath, indexed, authority, supportedAdapterVersions, now=Date.now())` with the identity/catalog/digest refusals and the installed-probe/scripted-fixture origin branch exactly as the LLD's section 2.3 and reference [[c1]] describe. src/agent/providers/native-investigation-session.ts:19-22 defines `export function nativeReviewMcpConfiguration(cwd, indexed)` returning `{mcpServers:{'insrc-scoped-review':{...}}}` matching section 2.2's described return shape. [files: src/agent/providers/investigation-session.ts, src/agent/providers/native-investigation-session.ts]","action":"None — the design's description of current behaviour is accurate.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The sibling IPC methods (`codeReview.investigation`, `codeReview.diagnostics`, `codeReview.investigation.capabilities`) are registered in buildHandlerRuntime (handler-runtime.ts) and pinned to the main daemon via MAIN_DAEMON_CONNECTION_METHODS in method-class.ts, as cited at [[c6]]/[[c7]], which the new probe method is designed to follow.","evidence":"src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts:608-614 registers 'codeReview.investigation.capabilities', 'codeReview.diagnostics', 'codeReview.investigation' as session handlers delegating to review-investigation-gateway.js; src/daemon/threads/method-class.ts:88-91 classifies them 'session' and line 283 lists 'codeReview.investigation','codeReview.investigation.capabilities','codeReview.diagnostics' in MAIN_DAEMON_CONNECTION_METHODS. [files: src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/daemon/threads/method-class.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The listed call sites for the new `codeReview.investigation.probe` IPC (section 3.1: cli-provider.ts, native-investigation-session.ts, review-investigation-adoption.ts, handler-runtime.ts, method-class.ts) are complete — i.e. no other existing module that implements the sibling investigation-IPC handler logic needs to change.","evidence":"The sibling methods the design says to follow ('codeReview.investigation', 'codeReview.diagnostics', 'codeReview.investigation.capabilities') are not implemented inline in handler-runtime.ts — they delegate via `await import('./review-investigation-gateway.js')` to `dispatchInvestigation` / `investigationTransport` / `legacyInvestigationDiagnostics` / `investigationCapabilities`, all defined in src/daemon/review-investigation-gateway.ts (confirmed by reading that file's exports). Section 3.1's change-site list omits src/daemon/review-investigation-gateway.ts even though it is exactly where 'the existing investigation siblings' pattern the design cites puts its handler logic, so the list of files to change for the new start/status/cancel/export operations is incomplete. [files: src/daemon/review-investigation-gateway.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts]","action":"Add src/daemon/review-investigation-gateway.ts (or name the equivalent new module) to the Data-model-change call sites so the probe dispatch logic has a designated home consistent with the sibling pattern.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Invariant [[c1]] — 'Qualification accepts installed evidence only after independent verification; scripted fixtures cannot upgrade to installed proof' — is true of the current implementation and the new probe path (which only emits unsigned, non-schema-conforming observation envelopes) does not weaken it.","evidence":"src/agent/providers/investigation-session.ts:98-100: `if(authority.origin==='installed-probe'){ if(!authority.verifyInstalled)refuse(...); await authority.verifyInstalled(...); } else if(authority.origin!=='scripted-fixture') refuse(...)`. Independently, src/daemon/review-investigation-adoption.ts:33 defines the production-adoption schema as `z.object({version:z.literal(1), kind:z.literal('review-investigation-installed-probe'), origin:z.literal('installed-probe'), ...}).strict()` — production adoption structurally rejects any payload whose origin is not literally 'installed-probe', so scripted-fixture evidence cannot reach production qualification regardless of the new probe's unsigned-observation output (which the LLD states is explicitly never treated as NativeIsolationEvidence candidate without independent signing). [files: src/agent/providers/investigation-session.ts, src/daemon/review-investigation-adoption.ts]","action":"None — the invariant holds in the current code and the new unsigned-observation envelope is kept outside the signed-evidence schema the invariant depends on.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion (ac1-ac5) has a mapped test whose subject would fail under today's code, since no live probe producer, no operator probe IPC, and no unsigned-observation schema currently exist.","evidence":"ISSUE-7aaf7e1b4a54e86f.json body.reproduction/rootCause states plainly: 'no live probe execution/issuance path is supplied' and 'Supplemental filesystem search finds no real installed-probe runner/issuer.' The LLD's acceptance-mapping table ties ac1 (bounded trusted probe grant, one attempt, global serialization), ac2 (independently supported observations or explicit unsupported), ac3 (two ACKs + cancellation/process-group teardown), ac4 (signed-evidence + canonical approval gate, no bypass) and ac5 (post-approval real acceptance with exact CR/receipt) each to a named proving test under a test level (unit/integration/live) that exercises code which does not yet exist, so each would fail (or not compile/route) against current code absent the described build. [files: .insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-7aaf7e1b4a54e86f.json]","action":"None at the design stage — the test-to-criterion mapping is plausible and grounded in the confirmed absence of the current probe path; actual pass/fail determination is a build-time (code-review) concern, not a design-time one.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":1,"low":5,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-29T19:45:08.356Z","model":"cli-claude:claude-sonnet-5","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
